A||N||18||jaguiler||A/C - more questions!  I'm getting hot!!||||5||
Z||000000||jaguiler||05-16-2001||06:36 PM||||"If you reach down to the front of the compressor. (Engine shut off of course) If you can turn the compressor (center of pulley and not the pulley ifself then the compressor is probably alright. If the center does not turn the compressor is shot."<P>- I tried this and the piece does turn....<BR>still hot air....<P>"I believe that switch is a low pressure switch that keeps the compressor from running when the system is discharged... If so, you usually have to jumper them to get the compressor to run in a discharged system long enough to build the charge up."<P>-This quote is talking about the switch on the accumulator in the front compartment.  I grounded them together and sure enough my compressor runs great! no noise....belt is tight...  I left it running for a couple mintues ....still hot air....<BR>My pressure is around 25-30psi on the low side..... still hot air....<BR>does grounding this switch and the compressor working mean that my compressor is good??<P>Also I read somewhere about the relays on the drivers side firewall.... if these are bad will it affect me?  I ahve not tested them yet.... not sure how too....<P>I have not lost any refridgerant since the last time I charged it either....  <BR>I remember the last time I looked at the compressor on a hot day...I noticed the comepressor would engage for a few seconds and then shut off...it would do this every couple mintues..... is this normal? a mechanic told me it should engage for abnout 30 seconds at a time.....<P>Pleasse help...Baltimroe gets very hot!!<P>Thanks you all!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||5
