Z||000018||thomas_l||05-18-2001||01:18 PM||||A/C is pretty simple - if you have 26-30 psi on the low side and around 200 on the high side, <I>something</I> is getting cold. Let the system run a while with good gauge readings and inpect the system for frosted lines (low-side restriction) or red hot lines (hi-side restriction). If all is well, the accumulator and lines in and out of the evaporator should be cold. In that case, make sure your blend doors are working and not letting the cold air pass over the heater core. Not having screwed with mine (heater core bypassed by last owner  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) I don't know where the heater control valve is offhand.||||reg||1
